# Voice Pipeline

- The pipeline is microphone -> STT -> language engine -> TTS -> speaker.
- Support partial transcripts and final transcripts separately.
- Prefer streaming responses instead of full-buffer generation.
- Support interruption: if the user speaks during TTS playback, stop TTS quickly.
- Keep turn state explicit and testable.
- Apple Speech or SpeechAnalyzer should be the default STT path first.
- WhisperKit can be used as an alternative or fallback STT engine.
- Kokoro is the high-quality TTS engine; Apple TTS can be used as fallback.
- Do not call STT or TTS frameworks directly from SwiftUI views.